{
 "standing": "Normative machine-readable registry for identity-and-evidence section 3. Every 64-hex field in this bundle carries x-opensip-digest; a field without one is not admissible. domainSets additionally name the owning contract admission that Run closure must re-run over the retained frame, the retained closure joins it must re-derive, and the snapshot joins its paths must satisfy.",
 "retention": {
  "preimage": "default: the exact preimage bytes are retained in the content-addressed store under this digest, and the closure checker fetches and re-hashes them",
  "fragment": "the preimage is a canonical sub-object of an already retained record; locatedBy states where, and the closure checker recomputes it there",
  "derived": "recomputed from another retained artifact by the stated recipe",
  "owner-retained": "retained and admitted by the named owning contract; the identity closure joins by digest equality only and does not demand the bytes"
 },
 "domainSetLabels": {
  "native-context": "NATIVE_CONTEXT",
  "native-semantic-universe": "NATIVE_UNIVERSE",
  "native-nested": "NATIVE_NESTED"
 },
 "languageModes": {
  "standing": "native-evidence LanguageMode -> the native universe language it requests. syntax-only requests the `syntax` universe: it requests no COMPILER universe, which is a different statement from requesting none at all. It previously mapped to null, and because fact2/subject-scope require a universe h-identity from a closed set of two compiler domains, the syntax and clones cells the capability matrix advertises for that mode - and every file/package/vcs-change fact in a repository with no TypeScript or Rust unit - could mint no fact and no scope.",
  "map": {
   "ts-tsconfig": "typescript",
   "js-allowjs": "typescript",
   "js-synthesized": "typescript",
   "rust-cargo": "rust",
   "rust-cargo-prepared": "rust",
